    "status": "partial",
    "summary": "Archived metrics can be recomputed from released result tables. These source-validated recipes describe a new experiment; exact historical execution remains incomplete until the listed environment, data and checkpoint assets are supplied.",
    "prerequisites": [
      "Obtain the experiment source, benchmark task data and frozen capability libraries. Website CSVs can recompute reported aggregates but cannot execute an agent.",
      "Follow install.md for local EOG gyms, Docker connectivity, Codex CLI authentication and Python environments. Authenticate with your own credentials; never reuse or publish saved authentication files.",
      "Run namespace packages from the repository root. scripts/env.sh adds the root, eval_service/sdk (simple_agentic_evals), and reference/gepa/src to PYTHONPATH. Install the reference project dependencies instead of substituting another GEPA version.",
      "EOG requires the reference EnterpriseOps-Gym runtime and its domain gym containers. Tools also require its ReAct/LangChain stack. Verify gym endpoints before spending the search budget.",
      "ALE requires the reference/agents-last-exam Python 3.12 environment, gated task-data including grading references, a Linux sandbox image and the historical task eligibility/exclusion snapshot. A current manifest can change the denominator.",
      "Freeze source, dependency locks, Python/Codex/Node versions, container digests, model identifiers, task/split manifests and library hashes. Current source fingerprints do not identify the historical runtime."
    ],
    "steps": [
      {
        "title": "Prepare an isolated run",
        "command": "# Run from a prepared writable experiment checkout, not the website.\nset -euo pipefail\ntest -f scripts/env.sh\nsource scripts/env.sh\n# Retain this tag for resume; use a new tag for each independent search.\nexport REPRO_TAG=\"$(date -u +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)_$$\"\nexport REPRO_RESULTS=\"$PWD/reproduction/$REPRO_TAG\"\nmkdir -p \"$REPRO_RESULTS\"\nexport EVOVLE_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-5\nexport EVOVLE_CODEX_TRANSPORT=stdio\nexport EVOVLE_CODEX_TIMEOUT_SEC=900\nexport EVOVLE_CODEX_MAX_EPISODES=4\nexport ALE_WALL_TIME_S=7200\nexport META_HARNESS_BACKEND=local\nexport META_HARNESS_CONCURRENCY=8\nunset EVOVLE_SKILLS_JOBS_ARM_DIR EVOVLE_AGENTS_JOBS_ARM_DIR",
        "notes": "New run using inspected current source. EOG timeout 900 seconds, four episodes, stdio transport and concurrency eight are explicit current settings, not established historical overrides. Append --dry-run to a search command to inspect its plan once prerequisites exist; preparation files may still be written. Recipes were source-checked and bash syntax-checked; no benchmark was launched."
      },
      {
        "title": "Search oracle-skills streams and evaluate final rows",
        "command": "# This arm refuses --jobs-suffix; use a disposable checkout without prior arm output.\ntest ! -e evovle_skills/jobs/oracle_skills_gepa\nfor stream in csm hr itsm; do\n  bash evovle_skills/src/scripts/run_gepa.sh \"$stream\" \\\n    --oracle-skills --final-row-only --model gpt-5 --backend local \\\n    --concurrency 8 --num-runs 3 \\\n    --run-name \"repro_skills_gepa_oracle_${REPRO_TAG}_${stream}\" \\\n    --max-metric-calls 50 --reflection-minibatch-size 3 --trials-per-task 1 \\\n    --seed 0 --max-retries 1\ndone",
        "notes": "Search uses task-specific oracle skills; held-out evaluation uses the full final library. CSM/HR end at v3; ITSM at v4. No ALE or earlier held-out rows are part of this arm. The outer run_oracle_skill_gepa.sh wrapper hardcodes the original absolute checkout; this inner launcher works in an isolated checkout."
      }
    ],
